abstract: >-
  A reproducibility report on the public Lean development yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028 (commit 3456e5e7): recompilation under Lean 4.32.0 (twice) and 4.32.2,
  axiom audit and the supplier's verification scripts, an export of the proof closure submitted to nanoda (capacity panic, no verdict; an instrumented run finished 187924 of 187925 items), nano-lean (187925 items attempted, 0 failures), logos-kernel (code 0, 180988 declarations reported accepted) and lean4lean (9465 of 9470 modules at code 0 when read on 12 November 2026, 05:20 CET; five pending), a replay of the fast controls by a non-author,
  two neutral observations on the repository, and a partial port to Lean 4.35.0 that was stopped. The checked proposition is an existence statement; nothing concerns a mass gap.
  Not refereed; no human has checked the proofs; no priority claim.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
